+# Marble Oracle 0.4.8.5 — AUGURSPEX layout repair
+
+**13 November 2026 — targeted repair of user-reported defects in 0.4.8.4.**
+
+## What was actually changed
+
+1. **Chart selector now operates on sourced display positions rather than saved slots.** The user's nine assigned market slots remain untouched. When only saved slot nine has real history, choosing CHARTS = 1 shows that market in the first visible card, rather than leaving a blank viewport. CHARTS = 1/2/4/6/9 means the **maximum number of sourced charts to show**, not a promise that that number of markets can be fetched. The interface visibly says `X DISPLAYED / Y REQUESTED`.
+2. **Responsive sizing replaces the hard-coded 405px chart rows.** The pure `chart_grid_plan` function uses the actual chart viewport and visible count. One chart grows to the available height and width; wider windows support two columns; smaller views scroll vertically to keep full-size labels/axes.
+3. **Date and price labels now reserve distinct space.** Date labels are selected using actual font measurement with collision rejection, and the duplicate observation note was removed from the canvas. Observation counts remain in the source/info footer. Prices retain a separate right-axis band.
+4. **Source detail and assignment remain tied to saved market slot IDs.** Changing the screen order does not reassign the user's persisted markets. Sourced-only filtering still hides charts without verified real history and does not delete or alter the saved watchlist.
+5. **Status and provider labels fit compact windows.** Visible one-line status messages are shortened according to available width; untruncated diagnostic text is still in state/SOURCE DETAILS. The selector variable now updates even when the callback is invoked programmatically.
+6. **Close-only history remains explicitly labelled** in the chart source/info footer, with line plots rather than fabricated OHLC candles.
+
+## Measured, rendered fixture results
+
+At **1400×870** (actual chart canvas sizes, pixels):
+
+| Requested charts | First chart plot |
+|---|---|
+| 1 | 1046×496 |
+| 4 | 508×218 |
+| 9 | 508×215 |
+
+At **900×580**, one chart plot is 546×237; the nine-chart arrangement uses 546×229 plots and scrolls. All measurements used synthetic, clearly labelled GUI fixtures, not live financial data.
+
+Additional fixture: with only saved slot nine having valid history, the one-chart setting renders that slot and reports `1 DISPLAYED / 1 REQUESTED`; the nine-chart setting renders the same one chart and reports `1 DISPLAYED / 9 REQUESTED`.
+
+## Verification performed
+
+- `test_augurspex_chart_repair_0485.py` — chart-count selection, sparse saved indices, persistence, actual pixel dimensions, 3 window sizes, chart text bounding-box collisions, no deleted watchlist: **PASS**.
+- `test_augurspex_sourced_layout_0484.py` — updated previous test for the new distinction between screen index and saved slot index: **PASS**.
+- `test_augurspex_readability_0481.py`, `test_augurspex_scrollable_0483.py`, `test_augurspex_native_tab.py`, `test_augurspex_grid_contrast_0480.py`, `test_augurspex_chart_axes_and_history.py`, `test_augurspex_source_details_gui_0478.py`, `test_tab_layout.py`, `test_no_news_or_markets.py`, `test_augurspex_integration.py`, and `test_augurspex_home_carousel.py` — focused checks run (see final handover for statuses).
+- Release manifest, SHA-256 inventory and critical assets revalidated using `Application/Tools/verify_release.py`. ZIP verified from clean extraction.
+
+**What has not been proven:** Actual user monitor DPI/font rendering on Linux Mint and Windows; unrestricted ASX/JPX/KRX/US price history; physical GPU/FFmpeg hardware regressions. External providers and converter engines were **not modified**.
+
+## Important files
+
